exercises.prompt:
Write `contrast_ratio(colour_a, colour_b)` for colours given as `"#rrggbb"` (hex digits in either case). Following WCAG 2:

1. convert each channel to $[0, 1]$ by dividing by 255, then to linear light: $c/12.92$ if $c \le 0.04045$, else $\left((c + 0.055)/1.055\right)^{2.4}$;
2. relative luminance $L = 0.2126R + 0.7152G + 0.0722B$;
3. contrast ratio $(L_{\text{lighter}} + 0.05) / (L_{\text{darker}} + 0.05)$, so the order of the arguments does not matter.

The tests check, among other things, that black on white is 21:1 and that `#777777` on white just fails the 4.5:1 rule for text.

